IMPORT prelude

-- Business Trusts Act 2004 (Singapore) -- the trustee-manager (s 6), its duties and its directors' duties (ss 10, 11), conflicts
-- (s 12), exemption clauses (s 29), removal (s 20), and the unitholder's position: limited liability (s 32), distributions
-- (ss 33 to 35), civil claims (s 40), compulsory acquisition (s 40A), winding up (s 45) and voting (ss 58, 63).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BTA2004.txt (amendments to
-- Act 30 of 2022, in force 12 March 2024).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 20 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the trustee-manager's duties
-- and the unitholder's position. Not encoded: registration (Part 2), change of trustee-manager beyond s 20, MAS directions,
-- indemnification of officers, the trust deed contents (s 28), oppression and derivative actions (ss 41 to 43), court
-- winding up beyond s 46(2), deregistration, meetings procedure, registers, accounts and audit, and the prescribed board
-- composition (in regulations, not retrieved).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Business Trusts Act 2004 -- unitholders`

§§ `6 -- who may be trustee-manager`

-- s 6(1): only "a company (not being an exempt private company)". (3): the trustee-manager "must not carry on any business
-- other than the management and operation of the registered business trust".
DECLARE Candidate IS ONE OF
    `a public company`
    `a non-exempt private company`
    `an exempt private company`
    `an individual`
    `a limited liability partnership`

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate, `carries on another business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate may act as trustee-manager` IF
        (NOT `carries on another business`)
    AND CONSIDER `the candidate`
        WHEN `a public company` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a non-exempt private company` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `10, 11 -- duties`

-- s 10(2): the trustee-manager must "(a) act in the best interests of all the unitholders ... as a whole; and (b) give priority to
-- the interests of all the unitholders ... over its own interests" in a conflict. (5): breach makes it liable to the unitholders
-- for its profit or their damage, and an offence ($100,000).
-- s 11(1)(b): a DIRECTOR of the trustee-manager must "give priority to the interests of all the unitholders ... over the interests
-- of the trustee-manager" -- the very company of which they are a director. (3): this "overrides any conflicting duty of the
-- director under section 157 of the Companies Act 1967". (4): no civil or criminal proceedings lie against the director for
-- breach of a duty to the company "if such act or omission was required by subsection (1)".
-- (6): but unitholders may not sue a director for breach of s 11 "except to the extent and in the manner provided for under
-- sections 41 and 42" (oppression and derivative actions).
DECLARE Conflict HAS
    `the director preferred the unitholders` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act harmed the trustee-manager company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was required by section 11` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conflict` IS A Conflict
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director can be sued by the trustee-manager company` IF
        `the conflict`'s `the act harmed the trustee-manager company`
    AND (NOT `the conflict`'s `the act was required by section 11`)

DECLARE Route IS ONE OF
    `a direct personal action by a unitholder`
    `an oppression application under section 41`
    `a derivative action under section 42`

GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a unitholder may pursue a director for breach of section 11 by this route` IF
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `a direct personal action by a unitholder` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `12 -- interests of family`

-- s 12(19): "an interest of a member of a director's family is treated as an interest of the director", and "member of a
-- director's family" includes "the director's spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter and
-- stepdaughter". Parents and siblings are not in the list. (7)(a): guaranteeing a loan to the trustee-manager is not, by itself,
-- an interest.
DECLARE Relative IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `son`
    `stepdaughter`
    `adopted son`
    `parent`
    `brother`

GIVEN `the relative` IS A Relative
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the relative's interest is treated as the director's` IF
    CONSIDER `the relative`
    WHEN `parent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `brother` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `20, 29, 45, 63 -- unitholder control`

-- s 20(1): "Despite any provision in the trust deed", the trustee-manager may be removed by a resolution approved by "a majority of
-- the voting rights of all the unitholders ... who ... vote" at a meeting. (2): a deed clause requiring MORE, or allowing removal by
-- LESS, is void.
-- s 63(1): a special resolution needs at least three-fourths of the votes cast, on at least 21 days' written notice ((2) shorter
-- notice if a majority in number holding 95% agree).
-- s 45(1): "Despite any provision in the trust deed", a special resolution directing winding up binds the trustee-manager.
-- s 29(1): a deed clause exempting the trustee-manager from liability for failing to exercise due care is void; (2) a release
-- given by special resolution for specific acts, or on the trustee-manager ceasing to act, is not.
GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trustee-manager is removed` IF
    `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `days of notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a special resolution is passed` IF
        `votes for` TIMES 4 AT LEAST (`votes for` PLUS `votes against`) TIMES 3
    AND `days of notice` AT LEAST 21

DECLARE Exemption IS ONE OF
    `a deed clause excluding liability for negligence`
    `a release by special resolution for a specific past act`
    `a release by special resolution on the trustee-manager ceasing to act`
    `a release by ordinary resolution`

GIVEN `the exemption` IS AN Exemption
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the exemption is valid` IF
    CONSIDER `the exemption`
    WHEN `a release by special resolution for a specific past act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a release by special resolution on the trustee-manager ceasing to act` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `32 to 35 -- the unitholder's money`

-- s 32: a unitholder "is not liable to contribute ... or in respect of any debts, liabilities or obligations incurred by the
-- trustee-manager" beyond money they "expressly agreed to contribute" -- (2) despite the deed and despite winding up.
-- s 33(1): a distribution may be made only if the board makes a written statement, "signed by at least 2 of the directors", that
-- it is satisfied on reasonable grounds the trust can pay its debts as they fall due after the distribution.
-- s 35(1): on declaration, each unitholder is "deemed to be ... a creditor" of the trust for the distribution.
-- s 34: a creditor of a unitholder has no remedy against the trust property.
GIVEN `the trust's unpaid debts` IS A NUMBER, `the unitholder's unpaid agreed contribution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the unitholder's exposure` MEANS
    `the unitholder's unpaid agreed contribution`

GIVEN `solvency statement made` IS A BOOLEAN, `directors who signed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the distribution may be made` IF
    `solvency statement made` AND `directors who signed` AT LEAST 2

§§ `40, 40A -- claims and compulsory acquisition`

-- s 40(1): a unitholder who suffers loss from a trustee-manager's contravention of the Act may recover it "whether or not the
-- trustee-manager has been convicted". (2): within 6 years.
-- s 40A(1): if a transfer of all units is approved within 4 months by holders of at least 90% of the units "(other than units
-- already held at the date of the offer by the transferee)", the transferee may, within 2 months, compulsorily acquire the
-- dissenters' units.
GIVEN `years since the cause of action` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unitholder's claim is in time` IF
    `years since the cause of action` AT MOST 6

GIVEN `total units` IS A NUMBER, `units already held by the bidder` IS A NUMBER, `units approving` IS A NUMBER, `months since offer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bidder may compulsorily acquire the dissenters' units` IF
        `months since offer` AT MOST 4
    AND `units approving` TIMES 10 AT LEAST (`total units` MINUS `units already held by the bidder`) TIMES 9
